{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game","id":1477507,"title":"Suggestions for a MtA (M20) Game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-26T19:57:08-07:00","id":1477507,"title":"Suggestions for a MtA (M20) Game?","content":"In May or June I hope to start a MtA campaign and I am posting here to seek some general advice.<br /> <br /> In the campaign the characters will awaken. They will gradually find mentors and grow in power and awareness. They will also deal with scheming Tremere who scheme.<br /> <br /> To be specific, the PCs will discover that many of the things that have gone wrong in their lives trace back to vampires in general and Tremere specifically. The Technocracy will be secondary villains with vampires being the primary villains. Some of the campaign will involve the Umbra and spirits, but it will mostly be grounded in the real world. There probably will not be any werewolves, ghosts, or changelings. The game will involve elements of the old MtA Metaplot, but will not be about that story. A lot of should be street level stories.<br /> <br /> I have an outline prepared. Also, this is more of a flexible &quot;to do&quot; list than something overly specific.<br /> <br /> That all said, what would you suggest for a MtA (M20) game?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T08:11:30-07:00","id":1477528,"title":"","content":"Try finding the book &quot;Initiates of the Arts.&quot; It deals with absolute beginner Mages. It also has ideas for just the sort of campaign you seem to want.<br /> <br /> There was also a book on the war between the Order of Hermes and the Tremere. It would you tons of useful bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-27-2022, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T16:32:03-07:00","id":1477550,"title":"","content":"Since you're saying that \u201cthey will gradually find mentors\u201d, does this mean that they're Awakening as independent mages? Because I'm pretty sure that once they come into contact with the Traditions and they decide to join, mentors will be found <i>for</i> them in reasonably short order. <br /> <br /> Also, how new are the <i>players</i> to Mage? If they're new to it, I'd recommend <b>Mage Made Easy</b> from Storytellers Vault. You might want to go with that even if they're somewhat experienced, as it contains advice about how to run games featuring mages starting out as independents. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm assuming that they're not all going to Awaken simultaneously, as the statistical probability of that happening by chance is nil \u2014 though you could potentially get some mileage out of it <i>not</i> being random. If it's not simultaneous, then there will be a period where some of them are mages and others aren't. This normally isn't a problem because Awakenings typically happen in the character preludes, or are simply part of their backstories; but if they are to Awaken during the Chronicle, you'll need a reason for those who haven't Awakened to be involved in the story. <br /> <br /> Finally: remember that one dot in a Sphere doesn't let you <i>do</i> much. It lets you <i>sense</i> quite a bit; but that's about it. This can help with the transition from Sleeper to Awakened, as (aside from a bit of Wild Magic during the Awakening) the newly Awakened mages won't be all that different than their Sleeper compatriots. Unless you jump straight to Arete 2 and two dots in a Sphere, that is. But it can also be a bit frustrating to be a mage limited to uncanny perception, which would be a decent reason to skip over the \u201cone dot in a Sphere\u201d phase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T18:10:58-07:00","id":1477552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game?p=1477550#post1477550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you're saying that \u201cthey will gradually find mentors\u201d, does this mean that they're Awakening as independent mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I hope the chronicle will involve the PCs choosing a Tradition or Convention, and that will involve dealing with potential teachers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game?p=1477550#post1477550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how new are the <i>players</i> to Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>That remains to be seen, by who respond for my call for players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game?p=1477550#post1477550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm assuming that they're not all going to Awaken simultaneously,</div> </div> </div> </div>In my current plans, the PCs all experience the same Bad Event, which results in them Awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game?p=1477550#post1477550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally: remember that one dot in a Sphere doesn't let you <i>do</i> much.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I am aware of, and I am open to suggestions. I've not made up my mind but i will probably give the PCs a boost of some kind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T19:16:41-07:00","id":1477560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game#post1477507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the campaign the characters will awaken. They will gradually find mentors and grow in power and awareness. They will also deal with scheming Tremere who scheme.</div> </div> </div> </div>First suggestion, write one ruthless, powerful elder Tremere pursuing an agenda that has serious consequences if not stopped.<br /> <br /> This could be:<br /> Put a dangerous politician into high office.<br /> Burn down a forest as part of a fire ritual to gain power.<br /> Ritually sacrifice a sympathetic character.<br /> Summon something from the Deep Umbra that will unleash destruction on the world.<br /> All of the above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game#post1477507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be specific, the PCs will discover that many of the things that have gone wrong in their lives trace back to vampires in general and Tremere specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Relating to things going wrong in the players' lives pre-Awakening as a result of the Tremere... I would suggest replacing this with <i>one</i> sympathetic NPC. Have them framed for the murder of their one true love, their memories all jumbled up by Dominate 3. You can roleplay the character's grief, anger and fear in such a way that the players sympathize with their situation and come to detest the Tremere from the get-go. <br /> <br /> Players have an individual, subjective idea about their character's backstory. Even when it is agreed between you and the players, inserting Tremere machinations into the backstory of each character takes more work than whipping up the NPC, risks weakening the foundation of your story by creating interpretive inconsistencies and leaves questions about why vampires would waste resources and time (nights can be as short as eight hours in Summer, depending on location) subtly messing with the lives of as-yet-un-awakened mortals. <br /> <br /> I started writing this before your reply to Dataweaver, in which you mention a single bad event experienced by all, causing their awakening. As long as their is a logical reason they were all in the same place (or dream space) to experience the event, that is sensible. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game#post1477507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy will be secondary villains with vampires being the primary villains</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game?p=1477552#post1477552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope the chronicle will involve the PCs choosing a Tradition or Convention, and that will involve dealing with potential teachers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you planning to have some Technomancers be available as mentors and others be minor villains? One thing that fits in well with the &quot;street level&quot; focus would be a Syndicate Financier <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CGqgyjUcq1A\" target=\"_blank\">buying up all the available single family houses</a> and renting them out, making home ownership impossible for many. Picture a homeless mage sleeping in an ally, because the adjacent building is a node.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T05:08:52-07:00","id":1477581,"title":"","content":"The characters should be aided by a mysterious black cat (and perhaps other animals). This is actually the ally (perhaps ghouled) of a Gangrel elder that is fighting the Tremere even from torpor, but obviously must act through intermediaries to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T07:51:07-07:00","id":1477584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game?p=1477560#post1477560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First suggestion, write one ruthless, powerful elder Tremere pursuing an agenda that has serious consequences if not stopped.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a lot of this nailed down already, but I don't want to post the details here because it might spoil for the characters that they have to stop the Tremere Hedley Lamarr from chasing the people of Rock Ridge out so he can get some valuable land along a railroad right of way. The PCs need just a few minutes to come up with a brilliant plan...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game?p=1477560#post1477560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relating to things going wrong in the players' lives pre-Awakening as a result of the Tremere... I would suggest replacing this with <i>one</i> sympathetic NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit to Add: I had already planned to include such a character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game?p=1477560#post1477560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as their is a logical reason they were all in the same place (or dream space) to experience the event, that is sensible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan to use a hack of <i>Nighmare at Hill Manor</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game?p=1477560#post1477560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you planning to have some Technomancers be available as mentors and others be minor villains? One thing that fits in well with the &quot;street level&quot; focus would be a Syndicate Financier <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CGqgyjUcq1A\" target=\"_blank\">buying up all the available single family houses</a> and renting them out, making home ownership impossible for many. Picture a homeless mage sleeping in an ally, because the adjacent building is a node.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good. Thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 03-28-2022, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T07:52:54-07:00","id":1477585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477507-suggestions-for-a-mta-m20-game?p=1477581#post1477581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The characters should be aided by a mysterious black cat (and perhaps other animals). This is actually the ally (perhaps ghouled) of a Gangrel elder that is fighting the Tremere even from torpor, but obviously must act through intermediaries to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also good. Thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T20:44:55-07:00","id":1478115,"title":"","content":"Starting with 1-dot Spheres isn't a bad thing for this kind of game, just something you need to be aware of. Wonders and other stuff will help here greatly to give the players more punch when needed without any need to increase their Spheres too soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T02:26:25-07:00","id":1478127,"title":"","content":"I tend to have my beginning Mages dealing with mortal issues or local spirit court issues for the most part and we've gone entire campaigns with Arete and Sphere ratings not even hitting 3 and it can be a ton of fun. As said above if your setting them up against immortal blood sucking wizards they're gonna need substantial allies and Wonders pretty much out of the gate. Hell, we've lost beginning PCs to a single minor Fomor that got lucky.....though honestly the city council and the zoning department was their most feared enemy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}